This project implements a UAE-compliant double-entry accounting engine.

SOURCE OF TRUTH — in this priority order:
1. /docs/source-of-truth/Accounting Rules - inFINity.pdf
2. /docs/source-of-truth/schema.sql
3. /docs/source-of-truth/feature-spec.md (Module 1.1.A feature list)

HARD RULES:
- Never invent, assume, guess, or "fill in reasonably" any accounting rule,
  tax rate, threshold, formula, or business rule not explicitly stated in
  the source documents above. If something is ambiguous or not covered,
  STOP and ask the developer rather than picking a default.
- Every non-trivial piece of business logic (validation, calculation,
  workflow rule) must have a code comment citing which document and
  section it implements, e.g. // [Rules §1.3] no hard deletes, reversing
  entries only.
- Never alter schema.sql's table/column/constraint definitions to make
  application code easier to write. If the schema seems to be missing
  something the feature needs, stop and ask rather than modifying it.
- All monetary values are numeric(18,2) AED unless a document states
  otherwise.
- Do not implement anything from Module 1.1.B–H or later phases even if it
  seems related — this project currently implements Module 1.1.A only.